# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the fusion programme's WP1 jobs (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the fusion integration branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from here. ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the
# tag the integrator's build job produces from the integration commit (sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env); a commit of a file the image carries needs a new build and tag.
# These jobs add to the generated pack in scripts/ci/references/fusion-jobs (make_fusion_jobs.py: <ID>A audited attach and the timed ABAB of the one-core fold, lever id s1): the card-M job
# C1 that runs FIRST, the tree-fold variants (lever twins s1f2) and the trace_ms read of the ABAB.
# C1 (FIRST, card M only, soft): S1 on ONE card, byte for byte against the served Untilize + ArgMax + Gather and timed (optimisation/ttnn-op/shard_argmax).
# It settles whether S1 is a win, and whether the two-level tree fold beats the one-core fold, BEFORE any four-card time. Rows 64 (the packed block), 32 and 16; six data regimes (random,
# peaked, ties planted at every boundary the kernels cut at, all-negative, +-0, and infinities/NaN); each answered by torch on the read-back logits, by the served composition, by S1 with the
# one-core fold and by S1 with the tree fold; ids exactly, values bit for bit, the joined words against their own ids and value bits, and rows past `rows` zero. Then (--timing always: the
# numbers are wanted even if an edge regime differs) a captured trace of 24 launches per arm over 25 serpentine rounds for: served, scan (alone), fold1 (scan + one-core fold), fold2 (scan + tree).
# WHY FIRST ON CARD M: the tree fold's C++ (tp4_shard_argmax_fold2.cpp) and the words output of both folds were never compiled before this run: a JIT error, a hang or a differing byte shows here in
# minutes instead of an hour into a four-card attach. The device grid is READ from the card and the scan uses all of it (11 x 10 or 13 x 10); the report names it.
# READ: 'SHARD_ARGMAX verdict=PASS' (exit 0; FAIL names the fold, the regime and the row; NOT-RUN carries the compile error verbatim), then the timing lines: per rows served_us, scan_us, fold1_us,
# fold2_us and the folds' own costs (fold1_cost_us = fold1 - scan, fold2_cost_us = fold2 - scan), and 'SHARD_ARGMAX timing_verdict s1=S1-WIN|S1-NO-WIN fold2=FOLD2-WIN|NEUTRAL|LOSS' on the 64-row case.
# S1 is a win when the best arm beats the served composition by 600 us (the four-card ABAB measured 0.70 to 0.78 ms of trace_ms for the one-core fold on an earlier stack); the tree is a win when it beats
# the one-core fold by 40 us. DECISION RULE (ORDER.txt): FOLD2-WIN -> the -fx-s1f2 profiles for the audited attach and the ABAB; NEUTRAL or LOSS -> the generated -fx-s1 profiles; S1-NO-WIN or a FAIL -> stop WP1 here.
# ONE CARD SEES ONE CHIP: whether four chips of a mesh agree is the audited attach's job. A FAIL or a NOT-RUN does not stop the window (soft). Duration (estimate): 30 min (container timeout 1 h; the per-call
# watchdog exits 3 on a hang, then reset the target card only). CARD M ONLY, BEFORE ANY QUAD JOB: the cardm step runs one board; it never runs while a quad step holds the cards.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/shard_argmax/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--timing always
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
